WEBVTT

00:04:59.050 --> 00:05:01.117
But I began to ask questions

00:05:01.117 --> 00:05:03.655
and search out the usual things

00:05:03.655 --> 00:05:05.607
that I had been exploring before,

00:05:05.607 --> 00:05:07.140
like, what do the maps look like?

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.590
What do the graphs look like?

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.629
What does the data look like?

00:05:10.629 --> 00:05:13.025
And the maps of violence

00:05:13.025 --> 00:05:14.987
in most U.S. cities

00:05:14.987 --> 00:05:16.979
looked like this.

00:05:16.979 --> 00:05:18.643
There was clustering.

00:05:18.643 --> 00:05:21.981
This reminded me of clustering that we'd seen also

00:05:21.981 --> 00:05:23.724
in infectious epidemics,

00:05:23.724 --> 00:05:25.716
for example cholera.

00:05:25.716 --> 00:05:28.083
And then we looked at the maps,

00:05:28.083 --> 00:05:30.797
and the maps showed this typical wave